Even though I have been revamping content and attempting to standardize ABF, this update is complete rebuild of the mod from the ground up, from localization to the backend code. I felt it would be easier this way to create a sense of unity in style and consistency of quality when it comes content among many other things across the board. Sadly previous save games will most likely not be compatible, but now the mod itself will generally have less bugs, find itself more compatible/easier to patch with other submods, and more performance efficient. In addition to that I've added lots of new content and redunancies for existing content, to allow for a variety of playstyles and further replayability. 

